{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review BLOCK remediation: corrected the starting vocabulary (`bridge status` absent; bridge-status fully removed), named `_bridge_commands.py` creation work and all consolidation consumers, corrected the workflow failure mechanism, added the canary reconciler-ref fetch, and expanded file impact to 33 paths. Defined exact HEALTHY/PAUSED/RUNNING/STALE/FOREIGN/NEVER_RUN/FAILED exits plus canary CRASHED classification; omitted max-age now explicitly disables age failure. Defined explicit CI versus stable local environment identity, authoritative minimal ref plus one fixed rich file, observed-OID CAS with bounded retry and loud push failure, and the process-surviving-failure versus SIGKILL/OOM witness split. Status is now a fast read-only snapshot; the canary owns two-snapshot lease adjudication. Added RED verification for parity, no mutation, failures, fence classification, env isolation, canary escalation/ref fetch/no API query, and rollback-source selection. Accepted the advisory that a last-pass status ref is not a new cross-client lock: it is single-writer status data, while the existing pass lock remains the only cross-client lock. Deferred removal of the one-release GitHub API rollback option to a follow-up compatibility-window ticket at epic close."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786302388005037001,"uuid":"e9b81c2a-e96f-49a1-bfad-2df175d51de1"}